    "description": {
      "value": "<p data-start=\"2161\" data-end=\"2174\"><em data-start=\"2161\" data-end=\"2174\">(6th Level)</em></p><p data-start=\"2176\" data-end=\"2244\">You emit a stabilizing surge through a panicked or collapsing scene.</p><h3 data-start=\"2246\" data-end=\"2256\">Effect</h3><ul data-start=\"2257\" data-end=\"2409\"><li data-start=\"2257\" data-end=\"2290\"><p data-start=\"2259\" data-end=\"2290\">Reduce fear or morale collapse.</p></li><li data-start=\"2291\" data-end=\"2310\"><p data-start=\"2293\" data-end=\"2310\">Stabilize unrest.</p></li><li data-start=\"2311\" data-end=\"2409\"><p data-start=\"2313\" data-end=\"2409\">Convert part of the fallout into a small faction benefit (Unity, Soft Power, morale equivalent).</p></li></ul><h3 data-start=\"2411\" data-end=\"2419\">Cost</h3><p data-start=\"2420\" data-end=\"2445\">Spend 1 Surge.</p><h3 data-start=\"2447\" data-end=\"2464\">Clarification</h3><p data-start=\"2465\" data-end=\"2516\">This does not erase conflict. It prevents fracture.</p><h3 data-start=\"2518\" data-end=\"2530\">Pushback</h3><p data-start=\"2531\" data-end=\"2612\">If used to suppress legitimate dissent repeatedly, Noise increases.</p><p data-start=\"2614\" data-end=\"2651\"></p><p><em>Recosted 2026-08-23: this ability's earlier economy (Civic Charge / Strain / Resonance / Leverage / Administrative Pressure) is retired \u2014 everything now runs on Surge, Clarity, Noise, and the misfire ladder. The ability dialog's cost line is the truth; ledgers named here are narrative, GM-adjudicated, never a tracked pool.</em></p>",
